From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:35:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Add RTC node to the
 Surface Pro 9 group

The rtc-surface driver binds to the SAM/SAM function (TC 0x01, TID 0x01,
IID 0x00, function 0x00), but no registry group creates that device, so
the driver never loads.

On the Surface Pro 9 the ACPI time and alarm device (ACPI000E, _SUB
MSHW0217) depends on the SAM serial hub and has no time methods of its
own (_GCP is 0), so the clock sits behind SAM. With the node added,
rtc-surface binds and its time (CID 0x10, get UTC time) agrees with the
system UTC to within a second.

Add the node to ssam_node_group_sp9. The group is also used for the
Surface Pro 10, 11 and 12 (Intel); the SAM RTC has not been checked on
those.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index ef87965fc..3d17dfdcf 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -51,6 +51,12 @@ static const struct software_node ssam_node_hub_base = {
 	.parent = &ssam_node_root,
 };
 
+/* Real-time clock. */
+static const struct software_node ssam_node_rtc = {
+	.name = "ssam:01:01:01:00:00",
+	.parent = &ssam_node_root,
+};
+
 /* AC adapter. */
 static const struct software_node ssam_node_bat_ac = {
 	.name = "ssam:01:02:01:01:01",
@@ -373,6 +379,7 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp8[] = {
 static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp9[] = {
 	&ssam_node_root,
 	&ssam_node_hub_kip,
+	&ssam_node_rtc,
 	&ssam_node_bat_ac,
 	&ssam_node_bat_main,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_perf_profile_with_fan,
